# Every pattern here is explicitly anchored. An unanchored pattern matches a
# directory of that name at ANY depth, and a bare `capture/` silently swallowed
# the whole `packages/capture/` source package: every "capture:" commit up to
# 819121b held schema and docs changes only, and the crawler existed nowhere but
# a working tree. `repo-hygiene.test.ts` asserts no workspace package is ignored.
#
#   /x/   root-relative, this one directory
#   **/x/ deliberately at any depth
#
# The `**/` cases are the deviation from "anchor everything with a leading
# slash": pnpm puts `node_modules` and `dist` in every package, so root-anchoring
# them would stop ignoring build output everywhere but the root. Written as `**/`
# so the any-depth match is a decision on the page rather than an accident.

# Capture artifacts are sensitive (CLAUDE.md §3.4): they may hold response
# bodies, storage state, and user content. Never commit them. The scrubber and
# the §3.4 secret gate are what keep credentials out of them; this keeps them
# out of history.
/capture/
# The schema fixtures are a capture tree on purpose. Redundant now that the
# pattern above is anchored — kept as a tripwire if it is ever un-anchored.
!/packages/schema/fixtures/capture/
**/auth/storage-state.json

# Generated environments
/envs/*/
!/envs/.gitkeep

# LLM call cache (CLAUDE.md §13)
/.siteforge-cache/

**/node_modules/
**/dist/
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/.DS_Store
/.env
/.env.*
!/.env.example
